<page--header></page--header>

<page--root data-theme="default-roject">
<full--width--block data--page--block="">
  <full--width--area data--page--area="" contenteditable="true" spellcheck="false" autocorrect="off" autocapitalize="off" style="outline: none;"><h1>Update Boards</h1></full--width--area>
</full--width--block>
<two--columns--block data--page--block="">
  <two--columns--area data--page--area="" contenteditable="true" spellcheck="false" autocorrect="off" autocapitalize="off" style="outline: none;"><h2>When to Run</h2><div>Run this action:</div><div><br></div><div>- After completing a task</div><div>- When starting a new task</div><div>- At the end of each working session</div><div><br></div><div>Open <a href="../../boards/tasks.page">boards/tasks.page</a> to begin.</div></two--columns--area>
  <two--columns--area data--page--area="" contenteditable="true" spellcheck="false" autocorrect="off" autocapitalize="off" style="outline: none;"><h2>Steps</h2><div><strong>1.</strong> Move completed items from To Do or In Progress to <strong>Done</strong>.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>2.</strong> Move newly-started items to <strong>In Progress</strong>. There should be at most one or two items in progress at any time.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>3.</strong> Add new tasks to <strong>To Do</strong>. Write each task so it is self-contained - an agent or future you should be able to pick it up without asking questions.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>4.</strong> Remove tasks that are no longer relevant. If the reason for removing is non-obvious, add a one-line note in the history entry instead.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>5.</strong> Check <a href="../../boards/backlog.page">boards/backlog.page</a>. If anything there is now concrete enough to become a task, move it to To Do.</div></two--columns--area>
</two--columns--block>
</page--root>

<page--footer></page--footer>


